是,首相 第二季第8集

3
00:00:08,572 --> 00:00:11,576
-=破烂熊字幕组=-
翻译&校对：tpring
时间轴：色色

4
00:00:35,913 --> 00:00:38,942
盘根错节

5
00:00:40,816 --> 00:00:44,469
伯纳 我们伟大的政治家今天下午如何?
Bernard, and how is our great statesman this afternoon?

6
00:00:44,470 --> 00:00:45,753
他挺开心的
Well, he's very cheerful.

7
00:00:45,754 --> 00:00:48,122
哦? 他什么事这么开心?
Really? Where did he found to be cheerful about?

8
00:00:48,123 --> 00:00:50,572
这次质询他应付得很不错
Well, at Question Time he did very well.

9
00:00:50,573 --> 00:00:52,132
是吗 谁说的?
Indeed. In whose opinion?

10
00:00:52,133 --> 00:00:53,213
都这么说
Well, Everyone

11
00:00:53,214 --> 00:00:55,881
窃听议员电话的事他答的很精彩
was impressed with his answer on tapping MPs' phones.

12
00:00:55,882 --> 00:00:59,096
对 我听说了 可惜不是听你说的
Yes, I heard about that, but regrettably not from you.

13
00:00:59,097 --> 00:01:00,358
这...我以为没必要通报
Well...I didn't see any point.

14
00:01:00,359 --> 00:01:03,851
伯纳 我统筹整个政府保安工作
Bernard, I coordinate all government security.

15
00:01:03,852 --> 00:01:05,645
这个问题怎么没先向我汇报?
Why was the question not referred to me first?

16
00:01:05,646 --> 00:01:07,382
这是意外问题 临时加的
It was an unforeseen supplementary.

17
00:01:07,383 --> 00:01:10,112
这是意料之中的意外问题
Well, It was a foreseeable unforeseen supplementary.

18
00:01:10,113 --> 00:01:11,961
可答复不错啊
But it was a good answer.

19
00:01:11,962 --> 00:01:15,013
"尽管我极其重视下院的意见"
"Much as I respect and value the opinions of this house,

20
00:01:15,014 --> 00:01:17,590
"我必须承认 尊敬的议员们说的话"
I must confenss I have no desire to listen to the word

21
00:01:17,591 --> 00:01:20,490
"若非工作需要 我一句也不愿多听"
honourable members for any longer than actually I have to."

22
00:01:21,471 --> 00:01:23,418
哄堂大笑      你笑的吧
It got a quite good laugh.        From you.

23
00:01:23,419 --> 00:01:24,948
有我 还有他的政党
Yes, and from his own party.

24
00:01:24,949 --> 00:01:26,488
那些想升官的
The One's hoping to be promoted

25
00:01:26,489 --> 00:01:28,128
还是那些怕丢官的?
or the one's afraid of being sacked?

26
00:01:28,129 --> 00:01:29,717
这就全包括了
Well, just about all of them.

27
00:01:30,757 --> 00:01:33,573
我猜他矢口否认授权了
I gather he denied that he'd authorised

28
00:01:33,574 --> 00:01:35,968
窃听议员电话吧      是呀
the bugging of an MP's phone.        Well, yes.

29
00:01:35,969 --> 00:01:40,985
他没授权吧? 是吗? 他有吗? 糟糕
Well, he hasn't, has he? Has he? He has? Crikey!

30
00:01:40,986 --> 00:01:44,568
都在这了 伯纳 包括转录文本
It's all here, Bernard, including the transcripts.

31
00:01:44,569 --> 00:01:45,390
我们去...
Shall we...

32
00:01:45,670 --> 00:01:47,062
不能过一会再去吗?
Well, Can't we wait a bit longer?

33
00:01:47,063 --> 00:01:49,818
他这种自得其乐的机会不多
He doesn't get many moments of unalloyed pleasure.

34
00:01:49,819 --> 00:01:51,991
他也只配有这么多了
I suppose he gets all he deserves.

35
00:01:53,644 --> 00:01:55,331
快进来 汉弗莱      首相
Come in! Humphrey.        Prime Minister.

36
00:01:55,332 --> 00:01:57,162
我想谈谈您接受质询的事
I want to talk about Prime Minister's Question Time.

37
00:01:57,163 --> 00:01:59,697
谢谢 我接受你的祝贺
Thank you. I accept your congratulations!

38
00:01:59,698 --> 00:02:01,911
我答得很妙吧? 你不觉得吗?
Wasn't I brilliant? Didn't you think so?

39
00:02:01,912 --> 00:02:03,099
我不在现场 不过...
Well, I wasn't there, but...

40
00:02:03,100 --> 00:02:04,005
哦 汉弗莱
Oh, Humphrey

41
00:02:04,465 --> 00:02:05,850
我答得妙吧 伯纳?
Wasn't I brilliant, Bernard?

42
00:02:06,522 --> 00:02:08,164
我相信下午您的回答
Well I believe your replies this afternoon

43
00:02:08,165 --> 00:02:09,635
一定让他们过耳不忘
will not be quickly forgotten.

44
00:02:09,636 --> 00:02:11,139
我来讲给你听 汉弗莱
Let me tell you what happened, Humphrey

45
00:02:11,140 --> 00:02:13,418
第一问是关于内政部
The first question was about that home office cock-up

46
00:02:13,419 --> 00:02:16,792
典狱官短缺的丑闻 我答得天衣无缝
over the shortage of prison officers. My reply was Masterly !

47
00:02:16,793 --> 00:02:19,363
我说 "请尊敬的议员参考一下"
I said, "I refer the honourable member to the speech I made

48
00:02:19,364 --> 00:02:21,685
"我10月28日的下院讲话"
this house on October 28th."

49
00:02:21,686 --> 00:02:22,938
他记得您讲了什么吗?
Did he remember what you'd said?

50
00:02:22,939 --> 00:02:25,679
当然不记得 老实说 我都不记得
No, of course not. Neither did I, come to that.

51
00:02:26,580 --> 00:02:27,874
不过堵上他的嘴了
Still, it shut him up.

52
00:02:27,875 --> 00:02:29,652
接着是失业率
The next one was about our employment

53
00:02:29,653 --> 00:02:32,216
"就业部是否在玩弄数据?"
"Whether the Department of Employment fiddle the figures?"

54
00:02:32,217 --> 00:02:32,709
您是说
You mean

55
00:02:32,710 --> 00:02:35,532
定期重组收集数据的基础条件
periodically restructure the base from which the statistics

56
00:02:35,533 --> 00:02:38,026
而回避了公众视线?
have been derived without drawing the public?

57
00:02:38,027 --> 00:02:40,989
是啊 玩弄数据嘛      当然有
Exactly. Fiddle the figures.        Well, of course they do.

58
00:02:40,990 --> 00:02:41,851
我知道他们有
I know they do.

59
00:02:41,852 --> 00:02:45,088
可我说的是 我尚未发现确凿证据
But I said I'd found no significant evidence of it.

60
00:02:45,089 --> 00:02:46,401
因为您没问嘛
That's because you haven't looked.

61
00:02:46,402 --> 00:02:48,122
我们也没告诉您
And because we haven't shown you.

62
00:02:48,123 --> 00:02:49,476
我知道 干得好
I know. Well done Humphrey.

63
00:02:49,477 --> 00:02:50,937
然后又是一记阴招
Then we went straight on to a googly about 

64
00:02:50,938 --> 00:02:53,737
貌似攻击能源部的核废料处理计划
the Dept of Energy's plans for disposing of a nuclear waste.

65
00:02:53,738 --> 00:02:56,346
其实是想诱我承认 内阁已经分化了
The question was tried to get me to admit Cabinet was divided.

66
00:02:56,347 --> 00:02:58,033
是分化了啊      我知道
Well, it is.        I know that.

67
00:02:58,034 --> 00:02:58,657
所以我说
So I said,

68
00:02:58,658 --> 00:03:00,721
"我的内阁决议都是全体一致通过"
"My cabinet took a unanimous decision."

69
00:03:00,722 --> 00:03:01,967
因为您威胁说
That's only because you threatened

70
00:03:01,968 --> 00:03:03,867
谁有异议就开除吧
to dismiss anyone who wouldn't agree.

71
00:03:04,743 --> 00:03:06,546
结果果然全体一致了
It certainly made them agree unanimously.

72
00:03:07,702 --> 00:03:10,551
我每说一句 我的后座议员都欢呼雀跃
By this time, My back benchers were cheering my every word.

73
00:03:10,552 --> 00:03:12,034
哦 对 下一个问题是
Oh, Yes, then we had a question about

74
00:03:12,035 --> 00:03:13,876
为什么我们花了大钱的
why since we spent so much money on it

75
00:03:13,877 --> 00:03:16,694
反导弹导弹出厂前一天
our new anti-missile missile was scrapped as obsolete

76
00:03:16,695 --> 00:03:19,440
会全部因为过时而报废?
the day before it came off the production line.

77
00:03:19,756 --> 00:03:21,967
您又是怎么岔开的呢?
And how did you wriggle out of that one?

78
00:03:21,968 --> 00:03:24,205
岔开? 这是我最得意的一个
Wriggle? That was my masterstroke!

79
00:03:24,206 --> 00:03:26,209
汉弗莱 简直是神来之笔
My reply, Humphrey, was sheer genius.

80
00:03:26,210 --> 00:03:29,040
我说我们的政策没达到预期效果
I simply said our policy had not been as effective as we'd hoped

81
00:03:29,041 --> 00:03:31,054
显然当初制订错了
Clearly we had got it wrong.

82
00:03:32,309 --> 00:03:34,912
您承认啦?      是啊 很天才吧?
You admitted that?        Yeah. Brilliant! Wasn't it?

83
00:03:35,391 --> 00:03:37,636
立刻就让他泄了气
Took the wind right out of his sails!

84
00:03:39,415 --> 00:03:41,588
在下院里说实话总能唬住人
Honesty always gives you the advantage of surprise

85
00:03:41,589 --> 00:03:42,787
让他们措手不及
in the House of Commons.

86
00:03:44,307 --> 00:03:47,357
临时又会有人问首相
There was actually a supplementary the Prime Minister was asked 

87
00:03:47,358 --> 00:03:48,827
什么时候会让负有责任的大臣
when he would request the resignation 

88
00:03:48,828 --> 00:03:50,197
交辞呈
from the responsible minister.

89
00:03:50,198 --> 00:03:52,441
好办 我说我会要他辞职
Too easy. I said I'll ask for it the resignation

90
00:03:52,442 --> 00:03:54,314
"等他犯了错误 有人抓了现行"
"When he makes a mistake that could've been seen at the time"

91
00:03:54,315 --> 00:03:56,323
"而不是乱放马后炮的时候"
"and not with the benefit of hindsight."

92
00:03:56,681 --> 00:03:58,132
他们高兴得一蹦三尺高
They were on their feet cheering,

93
00:03:58,133 --> 00:04:00,569
手舞足蹈 议程纸满天飞
stamping, waving their order papers!

94
00:04:00,570 --> 00:04:01,590
我听说
I gather

95
00:04:01,591 --> 00:04:04,797
有个问题问的是窃听议员电话
there was a question about the bugging of an MP's telephone.

96
00:04:04,798 --> 00:04:06,867
对啊 这个可把大家乐坏了 我说...
Oh, Yes, I got a terrific laugh with that. I said...

97
00:04:06,868 --> 00:04:08,481
我知道 伯纳告诉我了
I know Bernard told me.

98
00:04:08,482 --> 00:04:10,068
我说 "尽管我极其重视..."
I said,"Much as I respect..."

99
00:04:10,069 --> 00:04:11,882
对 我知道 伯纳告诉我了
Yes, I know. Bernard told me.

100
00:04:12,459 --> 00:04:14,013
好吧 反正问的也够无聊的
Oh. Well, anyway, that was just stupid.

101
00:04:14,014 --> 00:04:16,532
我们干嘛要窃听哈利法克斯的电话?
I mean why should we bug Hugh Halifax's telephone?

102
00:04:16,533 --> 00:04:18,449
何必呢 他可是我自己的人
Happens to be one of my own administration!

103
00:04:18,450 --> 00:04:20,397
他们怎么会冒出这种念头?
did where they get such a daft idea?

104
00:04:20,398 --> 00:04:22,508
被害妄想狂      对 问题在于...
Sheer paranoia.        Yes, The only thing is...

105
00:04:22,509 --> 00:04:24,614
我说 我们何苦窃听大臣说话?
I mean Why should we listen in to MPs?

106
00:04:24,615 --> 00:04:26,906
无聊 愚蠢 自以为是
Boring, stupid, ignorant windbags!

107
00:04:27,598 --> 00:04:29,364
能不听我都求之不得
I do my best not to listen to them.

108
00:04:29,699 --> 00:04:31,256
他不就是个政务次官么
And he's only a PPS.

109
00:04:31,495 --> 00:04:32,918
连我都查不出来
I have enough trouble finding out

110
00:04:32,919 --> 00:04:35,468
国防部在搞什么鬼 他能知道什么?
what's going on at Prime Minister's Defence. What could he know?

111
00:04:35,469 --> 00:04:36,799
就是说
So I gather

112
00:04:37,079 --> 00:04:39,981
您否认窃听了哈利法克斯的电话?
you denied that Mr Halifax's phone had been bugged?

113
00:04:39,982 --> 00:04:42,814
当然 今天就这一个问题我可以
Obviously, it was the one question today to which I could give a

114
00:04:42,815 --> 00:04:45,571
清晰 简明 利落地说出实话
clear, simple, straightforward, honest answer.

115
00:04:45,572 --> 00:04:48,745
是啊 可惜 尽管您确实清晰
Yes, unfortunately, although the answer was indeed clear,

116
00:04:48,746 --> 00:04:52,593
简明 利落 您最后一个形容词的
simple and straightforward, that is some difficult in justifiably

117
00:04:52,594 --> 00:04:56,027
适用性却值得商榷
assigning the 4th term you applied to the statement...

118
00:04:57,255 --> 00:04:59,475
具体体现在 要如何联系
....in as much as the precise correlation

119
00:04:59,476 --> 00:05:01,882
您公开传达的信息
between the information you communicated

120
00:05:01,883 --> 00:05:04,514
和迄今为止已知的事实
and the facts insofar as they can be determined

121
00:05:04,515 --> 00:05:08,883
同时您的表述方法又造成了规模可观的
and demonstrated is such as to cause epistemological problems

122
00:05:09,229 --> 00:05:11,391
认识论难题 从而使其
of sufficient magnitude as to lay upon

123
00:05:11,392 --> 00:05:14,394
对英国语言的逻辑和辞义
the logical and semantic resources of the English language

124
00:05:14,608 --> 00:05:17,719
加诸了它们普遍无法承受的重担
a heavier burden than they can reasonably be expected to bear.

125
00:05:19,159 --> 00:05:21,689
认识论? 你在说什么啊?
Epistemological? What are you talking about?

126
00:05:23,127 --> 00:05:25,870
您...撒了个谎
You... told a lie.

127
00:05:26,926 --> 00:05:29,429
撒了个谎?      撒了个谎
A lie?        A lie.

128
00:05:29,747 --> 00:05:30,950
什么叫"撒了个谎"?
What do you mean, a lie?

129
00:05:30,951 --> 00:05:32,062
就是说您...
I mean, you...

130
00:05:34,045 --> 00:05:36,642
撒谎了 是啊 我深知
....lied. Yes, I know

131
00:05:36,643 --> 00:05:39,313
你们政治家很难理解这个概念
this is a difficult concept to get across to a politician.

132
00:05:41,032 --> 00:05:41,931
您...
You...

133
00:05:43,139 --> 00:05:44,888
对了 您没说实话
Yes, you did not tell the truth.

134
00:05:44,889 --> 00:05:47,232
你是说 我们真的在窃听他的电话?
You mean we are bugging Halifax's telephone?

135
00:05:47,233 --> 00:05:49,680
窃听过      几时停止的?
We were.        When did we stop?

136
00:05:50,188 --> 00:05:52,073
...17分钟前
...17 minutes ago.

137
00:05:53,154 --> 00:05:54,788
这不能叫撒谎吧
Well, you can't call that lying!

138
00:05:54,789 --> 00:05:56,701
您说诚实的反义词是什么?
What is the opposite of telling the truth?

139
00:05:56,702 --> 00:05:58,579
可我又不是故意的
But I mean, there was no intent.

140
00:05:58,580 --> 00:05:59,907
我从不故意
I didn't mean to deceive them,

141
00:05:59,908 --> 00:06:01,438
误导下院的
I never knowingly mislead the House.

142
00:06:01,439 --> 00:06:03,334
无论如何 您确实误导了
Nonetheless you have done so.

143
00:06:03,335 --> 00:06:06,257
不能怪我 我又不知情
Wasn't my fault. I didn't know he's being bugged!

144
00:06:06,258 --> 00:06:07,872
首相 人们认为您知道
Prime Minister you are deemed to have known

145
00:06:07,873 --> 00:06:09,715
按理该您负责
you're automaticly responsible.

146
00:06:09,716 --> 00:06:10,921
怎么没告诉我?
Why wasn't I told?

147
00:06:10,922 --> 00:06:13,942
大概内政部长不觉得有必要通知您
The Home Secretary might not have felt the need to inform you.

148
00:06:13,943 --> 00:06:16,543
为什么?      大概他也不知道
Why?        Perhaps he didn't know either.

149
00:06:18,174 --> 00:06:21,072
也可能有人建议他 您没必要知道
Or perhaps he'd been advised that you did not need to know.

150
00:06:21,073 --> 00:06:22,593
可我有必要知道啊
Well, I did need to know.

151
00:06:22,594 --> 00:06:25,024
显然 当时并不知道您有必要知道
Apparently the fact you needed to know was not known at the time

152
00:06:25,025 --> 00:06:27,303
您知道它的必要性 我们现在才知道
that the now-known need to know was known.

153
00:06:27,939 --> 00:06:28,519
也许
Therefore,

154
00:06:28,520 --> 00:06:31,703
给内政大臣作参谋的人认为
those needed to advise inform the Home Secretary perhaps felt

155
00:06:31,704 --> 00:06:34,344
鉴于他尚且不知道他有必要知道的
that the information he needed as to whether to inform

156
00:06:34,345 --> 00:06:37,040
是否该向最高权威部门汇报
the highest authority know the information was not yet known,

157
00:06:37,041 --> 00:06:39,787
因此没人授权将情况汇报给高层
and therefore was no authority for the authority to be informed

158
00:06:39,788 --> 00:06:40,658
因为知道它的必要性当时
because they need to know

159
00:06:40,659 --> 00:06:42,398
并不知道 也不必要
was thought that time not known or needed.

160
00:06:43,936 --> 00:06:44,877
什么?
What?

161
00:06:46,152 --> 00:06:48,860
我们不知道您会在下院否认它
We could not know that you'd deny it in the House.

162
00:06:48,861 --> 00:06:50,916
要是我不知道 被问到了当然会否认
Obviously I would if I didn't know and were asked.

163
00:06:50,917 --> 00:06:53,217
我们不知道您不知道的时候会被问到
We did not know that you'd be asked when you didn't know.

164
00:06:53,218 --> 00:06:54,635
如果我不知道
I was bound to be asked

165
00:06:54,636 --> 00:06:56,439
被问到的时候当然也不知道
when I didn't know if I didn't know!

166
00:06:57,885 --> 00:06:59,300
什么?      什么?
What?        What?

167
00:07:00,327 --> 00:07:03,124
当时的考虑是 不告诉您为好
It was thought that it was better not to inform you.

168
00:07:03,125 --> 00:07:05,527
您看 哈里法克斯是您政府的一员
You see, Halifax is one of your government team.

169
00:07:05,528 --> 00:07:09,292
因此当时觉得 最好不要制造猜忌
As such it was thought it was better not to create distrust.

170
00:07:09,293 --> 00:07:11,548
您有必要了解时 我们才通知您
We only tell you when you should be aware.

171
00:07:11,549 --> 00:07:12,303
那是几时?
When's that?

172
00:07:12,304 --> 00:07:14,994
现在就是了 因为您刚刚否认了
You should now be aware because you've just denied it.

173
00:07:15,946 --> 00:07:18,590
我得在否认之前知情才有用啊
It would've been helpful if I'd been aware before I denied it.

174
00:07:18,591 --> 00:07:20,640
正相反 首相 如果您否认前知情
On the contrary Prime Minister, If you had been aware

175
00:07:20,641 --> 00:07:22,874
您就不会否认了
before you denied it, you wouldn't have denied it.

176
00:07:22,875 --> 00:07:24,040
可我有必要知道
But I needed to know!

177
00:07:24,041 --> 00:07:26,820
我们并不总告诉您窃听的事
We do not always tell you about bugging when you need to know.

178
00:07:26,821 --> 00:07:29,474
您看 首相 有时候我们需要您不知道
You see, at times,Prime Minister, we need you not to know.

179
00:07:29,475 --> 00:07:32,088
你凭什么决定瞒着我?      我没有
Why did you decide I didn't need to know?        I didn't.

180
00:07:32,089 --> 00:07:33,532
谁瞒的?      没人瞒
Well, Who did?        Nobody.

181
00:07:34,157 --> 00:07:36,499
只不过没人决定告诉您罢了
It was just nobody decided to tell you.

182
00:07:37,587 --> 00:07:38,332
那不是一样
Well, it's the same thing!

183
00:07:38,333 --> 00:07:39,888
恰恰相反 首相
On the contrary, Prime Minister.

184
00:07:39,889 --> 00:07:42,711
决定向您隐瞒信息
To decide to conceal information from you

185
00:07:42,712 --> 00:07:45,100
责任重大 任何官员都担不起
is a heavy burden for any official to shoulder,

186
00:07:45,101 --> 00:07:47,511
可决定不向您透露信息
but to decide not to reveal information

187
00:07:47,512 --> 00:07:49,327
只是工作惯例而已
to you is routine procedure.

188
00:07:49,328 --> 00:07:52,614
汉弗莱 我有必要知道一切
Humphrey, I need to know everything.

189
00:07:52,615 --> 00:07:54,351
一切?      一切
Everything?        Everything.

190
00:07:55,789 --> 00:07:56,721
很好
Very well.

191
00:07:58,151 --> 00:08:02,723
本周文具采购清单 48包...
Stationery deliveries this week. Four dozen packets...

192
00:08:02,724 --> 00:08:05,523
得了 汉弗莱 别胡扯了
No, Humphrey, Humphrey, don't be silly.

193
00:08:05,860 --> 00:08:07,603
我是说重要的一切
I mean important things.

194
00:08:07,604 --> 00:08:09,783
谁来决定什么重要呢?
Who should decide what is important?

195
00:08:11,469 --> 00:08:13,691
汉弗莱 这个漏子你到底怎么解释?
Humphrey, How can you possibly defend this cock-up?

196
00:08:13,692 --> 00:08:16,130
正如您在下院里说的 我们搞错了
Well, As you said in the House, we got it wrong.

197
00:08:16,131 --> 00:08:17,289
是你搞错了
You got it wrong.

198
00:08:17,290 --> 00:08:18,045
我 首相?
I prime minister?

199
00:08:18,046 --> 00:08:20,517
我不过是个卑微的公仆 小吏而已
I am merely a humble servant, a lowly official.

200
00:08:21,527 --> 00:08:23,705
这是内政大臣的决定
The Home Secretary made the decision.

201
00:08:23,706 --> 00:08:24,727
你有什么理由
Can you think about a reason

202
00:08:24,728 --> 00:08:26,097
能让我不逼他辞职么?
why shouldn't I ask him to resign?

203
00:08:26,098 --> 00:08:28,655
恕我直言 首相 您不能逼他辞职
With respect Prime Minister you should only ask him to resign

204
00:08:28,656 --> 00:08:30,746
除非他犯错误被人抓了现行
when he's made a mistake which could've been seen at the time

205
00:08:30,747 --> 00:08:32,640
而不能因为马后炮
not the benefit of hinesight.

206
00:08:33,447 --> 00:08:35,259
不过首相 这次还有个原因
But you see the trouble today has a reason

207
00:08:35,260 --> 00:08:38,303
是您一时糊涂 亲口作了否认
because of your error of judgement in making this denial.

208
00:08:38,304 --> 00:08:38,681
什么?
What?

209
00:08:38,682 --> 00:08:41,671
您就不该否认您不知道的事情
You shouldn't have denied something about which you didn't know.

210
00:08:41,672 --> 00:08:42,487
这怪你
That was your fault.

211
00:08:42,488 --> 00:08:45,078
你承认有事瞒着我的
You just admitted keeping secrets from the Prime Minister.

212
00:08:45,079 --> 00:08:45,991
绝无此事
Not at all, Prime Minister.

213
00:08:45,992 --> 00:08:47,587
首相 体制能够完美运转
The system works perfectly well

214
00:08:47,588 --> 00:08:49,715
只要首相先通知公务员
as long as the Prime Minister tells the Civil Service

215
00:08:49,716 --> 00:08:51,979
他要说什么 然后才公开说
everything he's going to say before he says it.

216
00:08:51,980 --> 00:08:55,611
可如果他贸然说了什么
But if, precipitantly, he says something without first

217
00:08:55,612 --> 00:08:58,095
没有事先找我们核对 那他咎由自取
clearing it with our official, he has only himself to blame.

218
00:08:58,096 --> 00:09:00,799
不经核对 您什么也不能说
You must not say anything public without clearing it.

219
00:09:00,800 --> 00:09:03,986
恕我直言 首相 您得学会谨慎
With respect, Prime Minister, you must learn discretion.

220
00:09:03,987 --> 00:09:06,132
我不知道有什么可谨慎的啊
I didn't know there was nothing to be discreet about!

221
00:09:06,133 --> 00:09:09,439
政府中总有要谨慎的东西
In government there's always something to be discreet about.

222
00:09:09,440 --> 00:09:11,828
再说 我们窃听哈里法克斯干嘛?
Anyway, why are we bugging Hugh Halifax?

223
00:09:11,829 --> 00:09:13,138
他和俄国私通吗?
Is he talking to the Russians?

224
00:09:13,139 --> 00:09:16,857
不 是和法国 这严重多了
No, the French, actually. That's much more serious.

225
00:09:17,654 --> 00:09:18,346
为什么?
Why?

226
00:09:18,347 --> 00:09:20,242
俄国人早对我们知根知底了
The Russians already know what we're doing.

227
00:09:24,983 --> 00:09:27,298
可法国是我们可信的盟友啊
But the French are our trusted allies,

228
00:09:27,299 --> 00:09:29,075
不管你有什么意见 谁没有呢?
whatever you think of them. And who doesn't?

229
00:09:29,076 --> 00:09:30,307
不 首相
No, Prime Minister,

230
00:09:30,818 --> 00:09:33,601
其实法国是我们可疑的盟友
actually the French are our mistrusted allies.

231
00:09:33,962 --> 00:09:34,496
有鉴于此
That is why

232
00:09:34,497 --> 00:09:37,589
和法国直接对话本身
talking directly to the French is regarded as prima facie

233
00:09:37,590 --> 00:09:39,830
被外交部视为叛国行为
an act of treason by the Foreign Office...

234
00:09:39,831 --> 00:09:41,309
是他们授权的
who authorised it.

235
00:09:41,310 --> 00:09:44,775
我不知道啊      您...不知道什么?
I don't know.        You... don't know what?

236
00:09:44,776 --> 00:09:46,703
我不知道谁授权的 谁授权的?
I don't know who authorised it. Who authorised it?

237
00:09:46,704 --> 00:09:48,034
这里有回声吗?
Is there an echo?

238
00:09:48,627 --> 00:09:50,606
汉弗莱 谁授权窃听的?
Humphrey, Who authorised this bugging?

239
00:09:50,607 --> 00:09:53,299
外交部 我刚刚说了
The Foreign Office! I've just said.

240
00:09:53,300 --> 00:09:56,281
总之 言多必失
Anyway, the less said the better.

241
00:09:56,282 --> 00:09:58,286
您不觉得吗 首相?
Wouldn't you agree, Prime Minister?

242
00:09:58,287 --> 00:10:01,932
关于什么?      关于一切
About what?        About everything.

243
00:10:05,090 --> 00:10:08,180
显然 我不能拒绝下院委员会的质询
Obviously one cannot refuse to appear before a committee House.

244
00:10:08,181 --> 00:10:09,553
不能 汉弗莱爵士
Well, no, sir.

245
00:10:09,554 --> 00:10:11,865
显然 得告诉他们一切
And Obviously one shall have to tell them everything.

246
00:10:11,866 --> 00:10:13,863
一切他们自有办法查到的事
Everything they can find out from other sources.

247
00:10:13,864 --> 00:10:17,725
正是 可他们大概会问我
Precisely. But they are likely to ask me

248
00:10:17,726 --> 00:10:19,438
首相是否曾经授权
if the Prime Minister's ever authorised

249
00:10:19,439 --> 00:10:21,338
窃听议员电话
the bugging of an MP's telephone.

250
00:10:21,985 --> 00:10:25,965
那么 忠诚的公仆该如何应对呢?
So how should a loyal public servant reply?

251
00:10:26,425 --> 00:10:28,882
您可以说 这得问首相
Well, you could say it was a question for the Prime Minister

252
00:10:28,883 --> 00:10:30,938
或者外交大臣 或者内务大臣
or the Foreign Secretary or the Home Office.

253
00:10:30,939 --> 00:10:33,843
或者事关国家安全 您无可奉告
Or it was a security matter not liberty to confirm or deny.

254
00:10:33,844 --> 00:10:36,044
如果我岔开问题 伯纳
If I dodge the question, Bernard

255
00:10:36,045 --> 00:10:38,122
你知道他们接下来会问什么吗?
do you know what the next question will be?

256
00:10:38,123 --> 00:10:40,742
为什么我不能作出明确否认
Why will I not give the same clear denial

257
00:10:40,743 --> 00:10:43,058
像首相昨天在下院那样?
that the PM gave the House yesterday?

258
00:10:44,382 --> 00:10:46,336
那我怎么说呢 伯纳?
And what should I say then, Bernard?

259
00:10:46,337 --> 00:10:48,302
您可以说
Well, you could say

260
00:10:48,303 --> 00:10:50,609
首相对此知道得比您多
the Prime Minister knows more about it than you do.

261
00:10:52,341 --> 00:10:54,118
那人人都知道我撒谎了
Then they'd know I was lying.

262
00:10:56,291 --> 00:10:57,959
那您打算怎么办?
So... what will you do?

263
00:10:57,960 --> 00:10:59,394
我不知道 伯纳
I don't know, Bernard.

264
00:10:59,848 --> 00:11:02,523
我只是觉得你也该为难一下
I just thought you should be aware of the dilemma.

265
00:11:03,240 --> 00:11:05,092
来杯雪利酒吗 伯纳?
Would you like a glass of sherry, Bernard?

266
00:11:05,093 --> 00:11:08,073
好呀 谢谢(甜的)
Oh, yes, thank you. Sweet.

267
00:11:08,433 --> 00:11:09,698
只有原味的
There's only dry.

268
00:11:12,049 --> 00:11:15,786
对了 伯纳 今天上午BBC来电话了
It's incidentally, Bernard, the BBC rang this morning.

269
00:11:15,787 --> 00:11:19,094
BBC知道了?      当然没有 伯纳
The BBC know about it?        No, of course not Bernard.

270
00:11:19,438 --> 00:11:22,913
他们想请我上一个纪实专访
They want to interview me for a documentary

271
00:11:23,296 --> 00:11:26,241
广播3台的 谈谈政府结构
they're making on Radio3 about the structure of the government.

272
00:11:26,242 --> 00:11:28,277
天啊 您不会去吧?
Gosh. You won't do it, will you?

273
00:11:28,564 --> 00:11:29,655
为什么?
Why not?

274
00:11:29,656 --> 00:11:31,762
他们没准要您说话呢
They may want you to say things.

275
00:11:32,840 --> 00:11:34,937
广播一般就是干这个用的
That is quite normal on radio.

276
00:11:35,455 --> 00:11:39,591
不不 我是说有趣的话 争议话题
No, no, I mean interesting things. Controversy.

277
00:11:39,877 --> 00:11:41,546
话说回来 伯纳
On the other hand,Bernard

278
00:11:41,547 --> 00:11:44,263
澄清事实 人人有责
one has a duty to put the record straight.

279
00:11:44,264 --> 00:11:45,108
您是说您要去?
You mean you want to do it?

280
00:11:45,109 --> 00:11:47,556
当然不是私心使然
Well, not for oneself, of course.

281
00:11:48,335 --> 00:11:50,664
不是因为好为人师
No inclination for petty vanity,

282
00:11:50,665 --> 00:11:52,352
想要扬名立万之类
you know, being a celebrity.

283
00:11:52,353 --> 00:11:55,851
不过 做人不能谦虚过度
But... one can be too self-effacing.

284
00:11:55,852 --> 00:11:57,517
我们这些人不该抛头露面吧
I thought we were supposed to be faceless.

285
00:11:57,518 --> 00:11:59,266
上广播不用露面
They don't show your face on radio.

286
00:12:00,748 --> 00:12:04,429
他们说如果我不去 阿诺德答应会去
They've said if I don't do it, Arnold has said he would.

287
00:12:04,430 --> 00:12:05,932
也许那样更好
Perhaps that would be better.

288
00:12:08,136 --> 00:12:08,765
阿诺德?
Arnold?

289
00:12:08,766 --> 00:12:11,021
要是为我自己 我倒宁愿不去
For myself, I would rather not do it.

290
00:12:11,298 --> 00:12:14,856
可责任感不许我坐视阿诺德
But I think one's sense of duty compels one to see that Arnold

291
00:12:14,857 --> 00:12:18,295
被树立成优秀公务员的典范
is not held up as an example of a top civil servant.

292
00:12:18,296 --> 00:12:20,519
您得找首相批准
Well, you'll need clearance from the Prime Minister.

293
00:12:21,240 --> 00:12:23,005
对      不过那不成问题
Yes        But that won't be a problem.

294
00:12:23,006 --> 00:12:24,005
你怎么知道?
How do you know?

295
00:12:24,006 --> 00:12:25,945
广播3台嘛 反正没人听
Well, it's on Radio 3. Nobody'll be listening.

296
00:12:32,182 --> 00:12:33,764
首相      汉弗莱
Prime Minister.        Humphrey.

297
00:12:34,393 --> 00:12:36,485
请过目内阁议程 首相
The Cabinet agenda, Prime Minister.

298
00:12:37,206 --> 00:12:39,688
你的专访是今天吗?      对啊
Is it today you do your interview?        Oh, yes.

299
00:12:39,689 --> 00:12:42,315
有问题吗?      没有没有
Any problems?        Oh, no, no, no.

300
00:12:42,316 --> 00:12:45,341
应对刁钻问题的方法我倒略知一二
I have some experience in dealing with difficult questions.

301
00:12:46,263 --> 00:12:48,617
如果你敷衍塞责 绕弯子
If you're evasive or confusing on the radio,

302
00:12:48,618 --> 00:12:49,742
他们只会剪掉
they edit you out.

303
00:12:49,743 --> 00:12:51,125
你得说点什么才行
You've really got to say something.

304
00:12:51,747 --> 00:12:52,574
说点什么?
Say something?

305
00:12:52,575 --> 00:12:55,217
要说得明白 还要有趣
Something simple and interesting.

306
00:12:55,218 --> 00:12:56,755
明白 还要有趣
Simple and interesting.

307
00:12:57,579 --> 00:12:59,986
也许您能给我些建议 首相
Well, Perhaps you could advise me, Prime Minister,

308
00:13:00,735 --> 00:13:02,820
尤其在问题带挑衅性的时候
particularly if the questions are aggressive.

309
00:13:02,821 --> 00:13:04,491
那更好啊
The more aggressive is the better.

310
00:13:04,492 --> 00:13:05,932
听众会同情你的
That puts listeners on your side.

311
00:13:05,933 --> 00:13:07,567
不过 我总得回答吧
Nonetheless, I may have to answer them.

312
00:13:07,568 --> 00:13:09,495
为什么? 我提问你就从来不答啊
Why? You've never answered my questions.

313
00:13:11,120 --> 00:13:13,425
不不 这是两码事 首相
No, no, no, that's different, Prime Minister.

314
00:13:16,438 --> 00:13:19,052
路德维克-肯尼迪可能会问些
Ludovic Kennedy might ask me some

315
00:13:19,053 --> 00:13:20,816
内行的问题
perceptive questions.

316
00:13:22,546 --> 00:13:25,396
他的研究中提到 很多人想问
His researchers mentioned that  lots of people are interested

317
00:13:25,397 --> 00:13:29,609
为什么我手里集中了这么多权力
to know why so much power is centralised in my hands.

318
00:13:29,610 --> 00:13:30,886
很多人?
Lots of people?

319
00:13:30,887 --> 00:13:33,034
没几个人听过你吧 汉弗莱
Hardly anybody's ever heard of you, Humphrey!

320
00:13:34,145 --> 00:13:36,555
也许他们是说很多广播3台的听众
Perhaps they meant lots of Radio 3 listeners.

321
00:13:36,556 --> 00:13:38,277
这不是自相矛盾嘛
That's a contradiction in terms!

322
00:13:39,752 --> 00:13:41,695
好吧 如果他真说很多人想知道
Still if he does say that lots of people want to know

323
00:13:41,696 --> 00:13:45,130
你就说 "举出六个"
the answer to that question, you say, "Name six."

324
00:13:45,131 --> 00:13:46,101
保证他没辙
That'll fix him.

325
00:13:47,619 --> 00:13:49,575
他决不可能记得两个以上
He'll never be able to remember more than two.

326
00:13:50,251 --> 00:13:53,232
太妙了 首相 还有别的花招吗?
Oh, excellent, Prime Minister. Any more tricks?

327
00:13:53,233 --> 00:13:55,519
花招 汉弗莱? 这叫技巧
Tricks, Humphrey? This is technique.

328
00:13:55,904 --> 00:14:00,453
抓住一个词攻击 比如"频繁"
Attack one word in the sentence. Like frequently.

329
00:14:00,454 --> 00:14:02,641
"频繁? 什么才算频繁?"
"Frequently? What do you mean, frequently?"

330
00:14:02,642 --> 00:14:04,087
或者攻击主持人
Or attack the interviewer.

331
00:14:04,088 --> 00:14:07,457
像 "显然你根本没看白皮书 不是吗?"
Say "You've clearly never read the white paper, have you?"

332
00:14:07,764 --> 00:14:09,203
或者自己提个问题
Or else ask your own question.

333
00:14:09,204 --> 00:14:12,064
比如 "这个问题问得好"
Like "That was a very interesting question."

334
00:14:12,065 --> 00:14:14,663
"现在让我问你一个问题" 你瞧
"Now let me ask you a question." See?

335
00:14:15,461 --> 00:14:16,853
多谢您 首相
Thank you, Prime Minister.

336
00:14:18,808 --> 00:14:21,356
这倒提醒我了 我最近会
Incidently, That reminds me, I have shortly

337
00:14:21,357 --> 00:14:23,327
接受一个委员会质询
to appear before the committee to answer questions

338
00:14:23,328 --> 00:14:26,570
回答关于窃听议员电话的事
about the alleged bugging of an MP's telephone.

339
00:14:26,571 --> 00:14:29,331
对对 伯纳告诉我了
Yes. Yes, Bernard told me.

340
00:14:29,332 --> 00:14:32,394
你证实我在下院的发言就行了
Well, you'll just have to confirm what I said in the House.

341
00:14:33,057 --> 00:14:36,721
可那是撒谎啊      天知地知
But that would be lying.        Well, nobody'd know.

342
00:14:38,405 --> 00:14:41,768
"哦 我们编织的错综复杂的网啊" (司各特 1808)
Oh, what a tangled web we weave.

343
00:14:42,714 --> 00:14:43,877
汉弗莱 你非说不可
Humphrey, you must.

344
00:14:44,132 --> 00:14:46,187
不然就成了我撒谎了
Otherwise it'll look as though I was lying.

345
00:14:46,900 --> 00:14:49,007
汉弗莱 你得忠诚
Humphrey, you have a loyalty.

346
00:14:50,666 --> 00:14:51,970
我忠于事实
To the truth.

347
00:14:53,143 --> 00:14:54,920
抱歉 首相
I'm sorry, Prime Minister

348
00:14:55,596 --> 00:14:59,362
我不能参与这种卑鄙的欺骗行为
I cannot become involved in some shabby cover-up.

349
00:15:03,309 --> 00:15:05,680
反之 在对国家的
So whereas there must inevitably be

350
00:15:05,681 --> 00:15:07,459
治理过程中
some element of shared responsibility

351
00:15:07,460 --> 00:15:09,153
难免会产生某些共担的责任
for the governance of Britain,

352
00:15:09,154 --> 00:15:11,064
介于立法者
as between the legislators on the one hand

353
00:15:11,065 --> 00:15:13,538
和行政人员之间
and the administration on the other,

354
00:15:13,539 --> 00:15:17,173
在任何事件中 原因之于结果
the precise allocation of cause to consequence or agency

355
00:15:17,174 --> 00:15:19,770
或曰手段之于终局 其具体分界
to eventuality in any particular instance

356
00:15:19,771 --> 00:15:22,859
盘根错节 乃至于虚无缥缈
is invariably so complex as to be ultimately invalid

357
00:15:22,860 --> 00:15:24,241
难以承担责任
if not irresponsible.

358
00:15:24,242 --> 00:15:27,280
我明白了 不过您能具体谈谈吗?
Yes, I see, but could you be a bit more precise?

359
00:15:27,281 --> 00:15:29,616
我是问公务员系统在多大程度上
I mean how far is the Civil Service to blame

360
00:15:29,617 --> 00:15:32,210
要为失业负责?      对 当然
for the present level of unemployment?        Yes, of course,

361
00:15:32,211 --> 00:15:35,288
"失业"这个大而化之的媒体用语
unemployment is a single name applied by the media

362
00:15:35,289 --> 00:15:38,640
囊括了五花八门的社会经济学现象
to what is a wide range of socio-economic phenomena

363
00:15:38,641 --> 00:15:41,911
从政治上看 最明显的表征恰恰是...
whose most politically visible manifestation happens to be..

364
00:15:41,912 --> 00:15:44,153
对对 您能不能再具体些...
Yes, I see. Could you be a little bit more precise...

365
00:15:44,154 --> 00:15:47,185
不好意思 肯尼迪先生
I'm so sorry, Mr Kennedy.

366
00:15:47,186 --> 00:15:50,066
是您向我提问的 请让我回答完
You've asked me the question. Do allow me to answer it.

367
00:15:50,952 --> 00:15:51,872
谢谢
Thank you.

368
00:15:52,401 --> 00:15:56,030
实际上 全国失业登记处每周
Happens to be a current frequency of weekly registrations

369
00:15:56,031 --> 00:15:58,397
会按规定收到登记数据汇总
on the National Unemployment Register

370
00:15:58,398 --> 00:15:59,458
人们认为
which is deemed to be above

371
00:15:59,459 --> 00:16:02,903
它已经高出史上可接受水平
what has been held ought be an acceptable level.

372
00:16:02,904 --> 00:16:05,506
不过哪怕理清各种综合原因
But even separating out the component causes,

373
00:16:05,507 --> 00:16:08,490
更不用说为其单独归责
let alone allocating responsibility for them,

374
00:16:08,491 --> 00:16:10,733
在统计学上意义都十分微妙
Is a task of such analytical delicacy

375
00:16:10,734 --> 00:16:12,918
无法在一个热门
as not to be susceptible of compression

376
00:16:12,919 --> 00:16:16,294
广播节目的范围中 完整加以阐释
within the narrow confines of a popular radio programme.

377
00:16:16,928 --> 00:16:19,760
汉弗莱-阿普比爵士 非常感谢您
Sir Humphrey Appleby, thank you very much.

378
00:16:20,976 --> 00:16:22,553
如果这算热门节目
If that was a popular programme,

379
00:16:22,554 --> 00:16:25,194
冷门节目得什么样啊?
what would an unpopular programme be like?

380
00:16:26,288 --> 00:16:29,391
谢谢 汉弗莱爵士 太精彩了
Thank you very much, Sir Humphrey. Absolutely splendid.

381
00:16:29,392 --> 00:16:32,755
承蒙夸奖 讲的还行吧?
My pleasure. Was I all right?

382
00:16:32,756 --> 00:16:33,987
您真的不能
Well, Couldn't you have said

383
00:16:33,988 --> 00:16:36,312
多讲讲失业问题吗?
a bit more special about unemployment?

384
00:16:36,862 --> 00:16:39,723
讲什么?      比如...实话
Such as?        Well... the truth.

385
00:16:41,799 --> 00:16:42,484
有什么好笑?
Why do you laugh?

386
00:16:42,485 --> 00:16:47,272
亲爱的阿路 关于失业没人会讲实话
My dear Ludo, nobody tells the truth about unemployment.

387
00:16:47,273 --> 00:16:48,003
为什么?
Why not?

388
00:16:48,004 --> 00:16:50,633
因为人人都知道 失业率减半只需几周
Well, because everybody knows you can halve it in a few weeks.

389
00:16:50,634 --> 00:16:53,535
怎么做?      只要不发社保金
But how?        Cut off all Social Security

390
00:16:53,536 --> 00:16:56,185
给那些拒绝了两次就业机会的人
to any claimant who refuses two job offers.

391
00:16:56,186 --> 00:16:58,133
北方倒真有些失业者
There's genuine unemployment in the north,

392
00:16:58,134 --> 00:17:00,753
可南方遍地都是懒汉
but the south England is awash with layabouts,

393
00:17:00,754 --> 00:17:02,099
大批人大学一毕业
many of them graduates

394
00:17:02,100 --> 00:17:04,675
就吃救济和住房补贴过活
living off the dole and housing benefit

395
00:17:04,676 --> 00:17:07,626
还偷偷摸摸挣大笔外块
plus quite a lot of cash they pick up without telling anybody.

396
00:17:07,627 --> 00:17:09,093
您是说 不见天日的私活?
You mean moonlighting?

397
00:17:09,094 --> 00:17:11,080
光天化日还差不多
Well, sunlighting, really.

398
00:17:11,599 --> 00:17:14,362
大多数雇主都抱怨缺人手
Most employers will tell you they're short-staffed,

399
00:17:14,363 --> 00:17:17,131
可你要招扫大街的
but offer the unemployment street sweeping job

400
00:17:17,132 --> 00:17:19,040
洗碗的 那些人拔腿就跑了
or dish washing job, they'd be off the register

401
00:17:19,041 --> 00:17:21,165
骂他们"寄生虫"都来不及
before you could say "parasite".

402
00:17:21,166 --> 00:17:23,780
老实说 失业率只会越爬越高
Frankly, This country can have as much unemployment

403
00:17:23,781 --> 00:17:26,317
只要国家继续在社保金上烧钱
as it's prepared to pay for in Social Security.

404
00:17:26,318 --> 00:17:29,460
没一个政客有勇气改变现状
and no politicians have got the guts to do anything about it.

405
00:17:29,461 --> 00:17:32,593
这话录进节目就好了      那可不是
Oh, I do wish you'd said that.        I'm sure you do.

406
00:17:38,908 --> 00:17:40,818
汉弗莱爵士      进来吧 伯纳
Sir Humphrey        Oh, come along, Bernard, come along.

407
00:17:40,819 --> 00:17:42,475
要这个干什么?
I'm sorry, what's this for?

408
00:17:42,476 --> 00:17:44,301
BBC刚给我送来了带子
The BBC have just sent me this tape.

409
00:17:44,302 --> 00:17:46,005
似乎是我专访的录音片段
Apparently, it's part of my interview.

410
00:17:46,318 --> 00:17:49,763
他们说简直太有趣了
They say it's particularly interesting.

411
00:17:51,419 --> 00:17:52,680
您的专访?
Your interview?

412
00:17:52,681 --> 00:17:55,527
你不相信我能说得有趣吗 伯纳?
You're surprised I should said something interesting, Bernard?

413
00:17:55,528 --> 00:17:57,815
不不不 我只是以为您
Oh, no, no, Sir Humphrey, it's just that I thought you

414
00:17:57,816 --> 00:18:00,679
打算像平常一样 什么都不说 呃...
intended to say nothing, as always. I mean...

415
00:18:01,466 --> 00:18:05,040
打开听听 伯纳 你会受益良多的
Switch it on, Bernard. You may learn something.

416
00:18:07,048 --> 00:18:10,428
亲爱的阿路 关于失业没人会讲实话
My dear Ludo, nobody tells the truth about unemployment.

417
00:18:10,429 --> 00:18:11,571
为什么?
Why not?

418
00:18:11,572 --> 00:18:13,980
因为人人都知道 失业率减半只需...
Because everyone knows you can halve it...

419
00:18:15,768 --> 00:18:18,703
只要不发社保金给那些
Cut off all Social Security to all claimants

420
00:18:18,704 --> 00:18:20,599
拒绝了两次就业机会的人
who refuse two j'ob offers...

421
00:18:23,505 --> 00:18:26,504
没一个政客有勇气改变现状
And no politicians have got the guts to do anything about.

422
00:18:28,304 --> 00:18:30,117
汉弗莱爵士 这不是您吧?
Sir Humphrey, that wasn't you, was it?

423
00:18:32,376 --> 00:18:33,397
是我 伯纳
Yes, Bernard.

424
00:18:34,299 --> 00:18:36,370
可您怎能说这种话?
But how could you say such things?

425
00:18:36,615 --> 00:18:37,766
后面还有吗?
Is there any more?

426
00:18:47,326 --> 00:18:48,461
有 伯纳
Yes, Bernard.

427
00:18:49,024 --> 00:18:51,244
都这么有破坏性吗?
As damaging as what we've just heard?

428
00:18:52,927 --> 00:18:54,034
还不止呢
More damaging.

429
00:18:55,115 --> 00:18:58,370
我记得似乎说了... 寄生虫
I believe I referred to... parasites.

430
00:18:58,371 --> 00:19:00,488
您怎能这么不谨慎?
How could you be so indiscreet?

431
00:19:00,784 --> 00:19:01,748
访谈已经结束了
The interview was over!

432
00:19:01,749 --> 00:19:04,731
我们在聊天 这不是官方记录
We were just chatting harmlessly! It was off the record!

433
00:19:04,732 --> 00:19:06,111
都录在带子上了
It was on the tape!

434
00:19:07,223 --> 00:19:08,890
老天啊 我明白了
Oh, my God, I've just realised!

435
00:19:10,286 --> 00:19:11,574
敲诈      敲诈?
Blackmail.        Blackmail?

436
00:19:11,575 --> 00:19:12,484
念念
Read that.

437
00:19:13,457 --> 00:19:16,575
"这是您访谈中非正式的部分"
"Here is a copy of your off-the-recordpart of the interview."

438
00:19:16,576 --> 00:19:18,553
"我们觉得太有趣了"
"We found it very interesting."

439
00:19:18,554 --> 00:19:20,340
"我们将很快与你联系"
We will contact you shortly.

440
00:19:20,341 --> 00:19:22,127
他们想要什么呢 伯纳?
What do they want of me, Bernard?

441
00:19:22,128 --> 00:19:25,546
BBC? 收视费涨50%?
The BBC? Licence fee up 50%?

442
00:19:27,025 --> 00:19:29,288
没准是制作人私下里敲诈
Maybe it's a private blackmail by the producer.

443
00:19:29,289 --> 00:19:32,481
没准      他不知道我多穷吗?
Maybe.        Doesn't he know I'm a poor man?

444
00:19:33,466 --> 00:19:35,263
也许他不了解您那一穷二白
Maybe he hasn't read you live in abject poverty

445
00:19:35,264 --> 00:19:36,964
一年81000镑的生活
on 81,000 a year.

446
00:19:41,917 --> 00:19:43,738
伯纳 我该怎么办?
Bernard, What am I going to do?

447
00:19:43,739 --> 00:19:45,413
今后嘴巴放严实点
Well, keep your mouth shut in future.

448
00:19:45,414 --> 00:19:47,434
你也一样 伯纳
And so must you Bernard!

449
00:19:47,731 --> 00:19:50,133
不许跟任何人提一个字 任何人
I don't want you to breathe a word about this to anyone! Anyone!

450
00:19:50,134 --> 00:19:51,033
我有责任告诉...
My duty to the...

451
00:19:51,034 --> 00:19:52,180
伯纳 我会...
Bernard! I will...

452
00:19:56,662 --> 00:19:58,646
伯纳 我该怎么办呢?
Bernard, what am I going to do?

453
00:19:59,002 --> 00:20:01,045
也许您应该在媒体上发个声明
Well, perhaps you should put out a press statement

454
00:20:01,046 --> 00:20:03,416
对失业者表示同情
expressing sympathy for the unemployed.

455
00:20:03,860 --> 00:20:06,709
同情?      您就快加入他们了
Sympathy?        Well, you may be joining them any moment.

456
00:20:15,602 --> 00:20:16,523
怎么了 伯纳?
Yes, Bernard?

457
00:20:16,524 --> 00:20:18,213
抱歉 首相 您忙吗?
Excuse me, Prime Minister, are you busy?

458
00:20:18,214 --> 00:20:20,727
能不忙吗 汉弗莱马上就来了
I suppose I am. I'm expecting Humphrey in a minute.

459
00:20:21,089 --> 00:20:22,830
我得决定怎么向内阁交待
I've got to decide what to tell the Cabinet

460
00:20:22,831 --> 00:20:25,990
窃听的事 要告诉他们实话...
about this bugging business. Do I tell them the truth...

461
00:20:26,618 --> 00:20:28,302
还是咬定我在下院的说法?
or do I tell them what I told the House?

462
00:20:28,303 --> 00:20:30,234
恕我冒昧 首相
Prime Minister, if I may venture to suggest,

463
00:20:30,235 --> 00:20:32,008
您指望内阁怎么对您
Perhaps you should behave to the Cabinet

464
00:20:32,009 --> 00:20:34,229
您就该怎么对他们
as you would expect Cabinet to behave to you.

465
00:20:35,112 --> 00:20:36,229
有道理
Yes, you're quite right.

466
00:20:36,230 --> 00:20:37,875
我得咬定在下院的说法
I'll tell them what I've told the House.

467
00:20:41,554 --> 00:20:42,534
还有事吗 伯纳?
Something else, Bernard?

468
00:20:42,535 --> 00:20:45,177
对 有件事您有必要知道
Yes, there is something else you need to know.

469
00:20:45,456 --> 00:20:46,450
有必要知道?
Need to know?

470
00:20:47,875 --> 00:20:49,649
对 是关于汉弗莱爵士的专访
Yes, it's about Sir Humphrey's broadcast.

471
00:20:49,959 --> 00:20:53,514
无聊吧?      开始是的
Boring?        Initially, yes.

472
00:20:53,515 --> 00:20:55,324
后来渐渐有趣了
And then it livened up immensely

473
00:20:55,325 --> 00:20:57,254
他越来越口没遮拦了
as he became more and more indiscreet.

474
00:20:57,255 --> 00:20:59,201
汉弗莱? 口没遮拦?
Humphrey? Indiscreet?

475
00:20:59,202 --> 00:21:00,736
唉 他以为采访完了
Well, He thought the broadcast was over.

476
00:21:00,737 --> 00:21:03,715
就随便聊聊 可带子还转着
He was chatting unofficially, but the tape was still running.

477
00:21:03,716 --> 00:21:05,256
这种老套花招他都上当?
He fell for that old dodge?

478
00:21:05,257 --> 00:21:06,139
对 首相
Yes, Prime Minister.

479
00:21:06,140 --> 00:21:08,027
凡是麦克风
You should always treat every microphone 

480
00:21:08,028 --> 00:21:09,691
都应该当成开着的
as that were live microphone.

481
00:21:09,692 --> 00:21:10,618
他连这都不懂?
Doesn't he know that?

482
00:21:10,619 --> 00:21:12,646
据我所知 他不常上广播
Well, I don't think he's done a lot of broadcasting.

483
00:21:12,647 --> 00:21:14,599
老天 那他说了什么?
Oh, dear. What did he say?

484
00:21:14,600 --> 00:21:16,775
他说 失业率随时能减半
Something about being able to halve unemployment tomorrow

485
00:21:16,776 --> 00:21:18,760
只怪政府没那个胆
but the government hasn't the guts.

486
00:21:18,761 --> 00:21:19,732
什么?
What?!

487
00:21:21,411 --> 00:21:23,064
他不知道在录音啊
He didn't know he was being recorded.

488
00:21:23,065 --> 00:21:24,731
母带在BBC手里?
And the BBC has the original?

489
00:21:24,945 --> 00:21:26,351
你知道后果会怎样了
You know what this means, don't you.

490
00:21:26,631 --> 00:21:28,301
明早的报纸头条啊
It means all over the papers tomorrow morning.

491
00:21:28,302 --> 00:21:29,461
快想想办法 伯纳
You must do something, Bernard!

492
00:21:29,462 --> 00:21:31,148
首相 其实我已经解决了
Well, actually Prime Minister, I'v already done it.

493
00:21:31,149 --> 00:21:32,545
我刚和制作人吃了午饭
I'v just set lunch with producer.

494
00:21:32,546 --> 00:21:34,175
他是我牛津的同学
He and I were Oxford together.

495
00:21:34,176 --> 00:21:37,310
他根本没打算播出 所以我找他
He never had any intention of releasing the tape, so I got him

496
00:21:37,311 --> 00:21:40,675
要来了带子上不谨慎的段落
to give me the indiscreet bit from the master tape.

497
00:21:41,756 --> 00:21:43,004
这是母带?
This is the original?

498
00:21:45,942 --> 00:21:47,824
汉弗莱知道你拿到了吗?
Does Humphrey know you've got it?

499
00:21:55,458 --> 00:21:58,032
要我告诉他吗?      为什么?
Shall I tell him?        Why?

500
00:21:59,764 --> 00:22:02,294
他肯定很想知道      那还用说
I think he'd like to know.        I'm sure he would.

501
00:22:02,949 --> 00:22:05,264
可他有必要知道吗?
But does he need to know?

502
00:22:07,320 --> 00:22:09,601
您是说有人有必要知道 可您知道
You mean somebody needs to know, but now you know,

503
00:22:09,602 --> 00:22:11,196
汉弗莱爵士没必要知道
Sir Humphrey doesn't need to know.

504
00:22:11,197 --> 00:22:12,652
可您有必要知道汉弗莱爵士不知道
But you need to know Sir Humphrey doesn't know,

505
00:22:12,653 --> 00:22:14,033
可他没必要知道您知道
but he doesn't need to know you know,

506
00:22:14,034 --> 00:22:15,976
或您知道他没必要知道
or that you know he doesn't need to know.

507
00:22:16,667 --> 00:22:17,264
多谢了 伯纳
Thank you, Bernard,

508
00:22:17,265 --> 00:22:19,392
真是提纲挈领啊
I couldn't have put it less clearly myself.

509
00:22:20,271 --> 00:22:22,269
您想听听带子吗?
Would you like to hear the tape?

510
00:22:22,270 --> 00:22:23,093
这东西怎么播?
Can you play this?

511
00:22:23,094 --> 00:22:26,618
不 不是那个 我让他帮我转了一盘
Oh, no, not that. I got him to give me a copy.

512
00:22:26,619 --> 00:22:28,129
且慢 我说
No, hold on a minute.

513
00:22:28,484 --> 00:22:31,077
独乐乐不如众乐乐
I think this deserves a wider audience.

514
00:22:31,395 --> 00:22:33,548
汉弗莱应该一起听
I think Humphrey ought to hear this.

515
00:22:36,575 --> 00:22:40,626
喂? 是汉弗莱爵士
Yes? It is Sir Humphrey.

516
00:22:40,627 --> 00:22:42,615
无巧不成书啊
What a happy coincidence.

517
00:22:42,969 --> 00:22:45,038
请他来见我们 伯纳
Ask him to join us, would you, Bernard.

518
00:22:45,039 --> 00:22:46,877
稍等一下好吗?
Will you hold on a moment?

519
00:22:47,779 --> 00:22:50,721
首相 我告诉您的事都要保密
Prime Minister, I did tell you all this in confidence.

520
00:22:50,722 --> 00:22:51,492
当然 伯纳
Of course Bernard.

521
00:22:51,493 --> 00:22:53,428
我会尊重你的保密意识
And I respect your confidence.

522
00:22:55,938 --> 00:22:58,119
这事很严重的 伯纳
This is serious, you know, Bernard.

523
00:22:59,217 --> 00:23:00,611
对 首相
Yes, Prime Minister.

524
00:23:06,301 --> 00:23:07,342
汉弗莱爵士
Sir Humphrey.

525
00:23:08,512 --> 00:23:11,169
汉弗莱 快快请进
Humphrey, come in, come in, come in!

526
00:23:13,044 --> 00:23:14,694
电台专访如何啊?
How did your broadcast go?

527
00:23:15,313 --> 00:23:16,695
不错 还不错
Oh, very well, very well.

528
00:23:17,515 --> 00:23:20,515
你谈了什么?      就泛泛谈了谈
What did you say?        Oh, nothing in particular.

529
00:23:20,516 --> 00:23:24,254
我记得指出了某些事不容易
I think I pointed out some of the difficulties in allocating

530
00:23:24,255 --> 00:23:28,124
在政治家和公务员间归责的问题
responsibilities as between politicians and civil servants.

531
00:23:28,468 --> 00:23:29,875
你谈的很谨慎吧?
But you were discreet?

532
00:23:30,688 --> 00:23:31,785
干吗这么问?
Why do you ask?

533
00:23:32,586 --> 00:23:34,259
到底有没有谨慎?      是的
Were you or weren't you?        Yes.

534
00:23:34,260 --> 00:23:37,155
"是的"是有还是没有?      是的
Yes, you were or yes, you weren't?        Yes.

535
00:23:37,156 --> 00:23:38,414
小汉?
Humpy?

536
00:23:39,725 --> 00:23:41,231
您不觉得我会谨慎吗?
Wouldn't you expect me to be discreet?

537
00:23:41,232 --> 00:23:43,068
那当然      那不就得了
Yes, Of course.        There you are, then.

538
00:23:44,180 --> 00:23:46,806
好啊 这么说没问题了
Good. Well, that's all right then, isn't it.

539
00:23:48,416 --> 00:23:49,998
干吗这么问 首相?
Why do you ask Prime Minister ?

540
00:23:50,278 --> 00:23:52,576
没什么 BBC刚给我一盘带子
Well, It's just that the BBC sent me a tape.

541
00:23:55,756 --> 00:23:57,001
带子 什么带子?
A tape? What tape?

542
00:23:57,326 --> 00:23:59,079
你广播的带子
A tape of your broadcast.

543
00:23:59,080 --> 00:24:00,689
我觉得该请你一起听
I thought we might listen to it together.

544
00:24:00,690 --> 00:24:03,551
不行不行      怎么不行?
No, no, no, no, no!        Why not?

545
00:24:03,552 --> 00:24:05,853
讲的没意思      没意思?
It isn't all interesting.        Not interesting?

546
00:24:05,854 --> 00:24:08,005
内阁秘书向全国讲话?
The Cabinet Secretary talking to the nation?

547
00:24:08,006 --> 00:24:09,758
没多大意思
Not very interesting.

548
00:24:09,759 --> 00:24:11,330
你是说你太谨慎了?
You mean you were too discreet?

549
00:24:12,706 --> 00:24:14,169
放出来吧 伯纳?
Play it, would you, Bernard?

550
00:24:14,908 --> 00:24:18,016
亲爱的阿路 关于失业没人会讲实话
My dear Ludo, Nobody tells the truth about unemployment.

551
00:24:18,017 --> 00:24:19,202
为什么?
Why not?

552
00:24:19,203 --> 00:24:22,020
因为人人都知道 失业率减半只需几周
Because everyone knows you can halve it in a few weeks.

553
00:24:22,021 --> 00:24:24,462
怎么做?      只要不发社保金
How?        Cut off all Social Security

554
00:24:24,463 --> 00:24:27,644
给那些拒绝了两次工作机会的人
to all claimants who refuse two job offers.

555
00:24:27,645 --> 00:24:29,675
北方倒真有些...
There's genuine unemployment...

556
00:24:29,676 --> 00:24:30,259
汉弗莱
Humphrey!

557
00:24:30,260 --> 00:24:32,140
真对不起 我不知道啊
I'm terribly sorry Prime Minister.I didn't know!

558
00:24:32,141 --> 00:24:34,039
他们瞒着我 采访结束了
They didn't tell me the interview was over!

559
00:24:34,040 --> 00:24:35,567
乱开簧腔
The indiscretion!

560
00:24:36,411 --> 00:24:38,836
不负责任 还有吗?      没了
The irresponsibility! Is there any more?        No.

561
00:24:38,837 --> 00:24:39,725
有
Yes.

562
00:24:40,789 --> 00:24:42,118
接着放 伯纳      不...
Play it, Bernard.      No

563
00:24:42,119 --> 00:24:45,230
拔腿就跑 骂他们"寄生虫"都来不及
... be off the register before you could say "parasite".

564
00:24:45,231 --> 00:24:48,180
老实说 失业率只会越爬越高
Frankly, this country can have as much unemployment

565
00:24:48,181 --> 00:24:50,837
只要国家继续在社保金上烧钱
as it's prepared to pay for in Social Security.

566
00:24:50,838 --> 00:24:53,865
没一个政客有勇气改变现状
And no politicians have the guts to do anything about it.

567
00:24:53,866 --> 00:24:59,171
这是你说的?      这是学口技的
You said that?!        It was Mike Yarwood.

568
00:25:04,715 --> 00:25:06,329
这种事我可为难了
I'm in somewhat of a difficulty as to know

569
00:25:06,330 --> 00:25:08,201
怎么办呢 汉弗莱
what to do about this, Humphrey

570
00:25:08,680 --> 00:25:10,782
我需要建议      建议?
I think I need advice.         Advice?

571
00:25:10,783 --> 00:25:13,011
也许该放给内阁 听听他们的意见
Perhaps I ought to play it to the Cabinet, get their reaction.

572
00:25:13,012 --> 00:25:14,884
哦 求您      或者枢密院?
Oh, please!        Or the Privy Counsel.

573
00:25:14,885 --> 00:25:15,663
哦 别
Oh, please!

574
00:25:15,664 --> 00:25:19,278
不如给女皇?      上帝啊
Or... Her Majesty?        Oh, God!

575
00:25:19,951 --> 00:25:21,780
你知道这个上了报纸
Do you realise what this would made if it got into the papers

576
00:25:21,781 --> 00:25:23,444
对我和政府破坏力多大吧?
the damage would do to me? to the government?

577
00:25:23,445 --> 00:25:25,172
我可以说我弄错了
Well, I could say I got it wrong!

578
00:25:25,380 --> 00:25:27,236
我查证了 这不是真的
I've checked and it isn't true!

579
00:25:27,237 --> 00:25:29,587
可这是真的      我可以说它不是
But it is true.        I could say it isn't!

580
00:25:29,588 --> 00:25:31,547
没人能证伪 又没人试过
Nobody can prove it, it's never been tried!

581
00:25:31,548 --> 00:25:33,624
你要对公众隐瞒真相?
You well tell an untruth in public?

582
00:25:33,625 --> 00:25:35,628
对 为了您 首相!
Yes, for you, Prime Minister.

583
00:25:36,586 --> 00:25:38,169
我们可以发个澄清声明
We can issue a clarification.

584
00:25:38,170 --> 00:25:40,281
我觉得你已经说得够清楚了
I think you've already made yourself very clear.

585
00:25:40,282 --> 00:25:40,992
不 首相
No, Prime Minister,

586
00:25:40,993 --> 00:25:43,003
澄清声明不是让人说清楚的
a clarification is not to make oneself clear,

587
00:25:43,004 --> 00:25:44,986
是把人洗清白的
it is to put oneself in the clear.

588
00:25:46,870 --> 00:25:49,906
"哦 我们编织的错综复杂的网啊"
Oh, what a tangled web we weave.

589
00:25:50,895 --> 00:25:52,441
把带子给我 伯纳
Give me the tape, would you, Bernard?

590
00:25:53,133 --> 00:25:55,172
我有件事要告诉你
Now I've got something to tell you.

591
00:25:55,987 --> 00:25:57,198
这是翻录的
This is a copy,

592
00:25:57,994 --> 00:26:01,782
可这是原版 是母带
but this is the original, the master.

593
00:26:02,459 --> 00:26:05,623
您是说...      从BBC取回来的
You mean...        They were retrieved from the BBC.

594
00:26:06,101 --> 00:26:07,189
谁取来的?
By whom?

595
00:26:08,955 --> 00:26:10,333
情报人员
Intelligence.

596
00:26:12,001 --> 00:26:14,536
那么...别人不会知道了?
So... no one else will ever know?

597
00:26:14,537 --> 00:26:17,041
这得看我怎么跟他们说了
Well, that rather depends on what I choose to tell them.

598
00:26:17,557 --> 00:26:21,379
当然 我可以直接还给你 或者...
Of course, I could just hand over the tapes or...

599
00:26:22,637 --> 00:26:25,882
我可以先拿着 考虑一下安全问题
....I could hold onto them while I consider the security

600
00:26:25,883 --> 00:26:28,115
和政纪问题
and disciplinary implications.

601
00:26:28,574 --> 00:26:30,953
我可不想参与什么
I certainly have no intention of joining

602
00:26:30,954 --> 00:26:32,868
"卑鄙的欺骗行为"
"some shabby cover-up".

603
00:26:33,204 --> 00:26:35,588
这倒提醒我了 你想好怎么
Oh, that reminds me, have you decided yet what you'll

604
00:26:35,589 --> 00:26:37,303
跟特别委员会说了吗?
tell the Privileges Committee?

605
00:26:38,698 --> 00:26:39,947
对 首相
Yes, yes, Prime Minister.

606
00:26:39,948 --> 00:26:43,795
我想好了 为了国家安全
I've decided that, in the interests of national security,

607
00:26:43,796 --> 00:26:46,438
唯一正直的办法是
that, the only honourable course is to

608
00:26:46,901 --> 00:26:48,233
证实您在下院的说法
support your statement in the House.

609
00:26:48,234 --> 00:26:51,546
说哈利法克斯的电话从未被窃听?
And say that Hugh Halifax's telephone has never been bugged?

610
00:26:52,533 --> 00:26:54,035
说我没有证据...
And say I have no evidence...

611
00:26:54,036 --> 00:26:55,195
不行 汉弗莱
No! Humphrey!

612
00:26:55,196 --> 00:26:57,836
说政府从未授权过
And say the government has never authorised

613
00:26:57,837 --> 00:27:00,029
窃听议员电话
the bugging of MPs' telephones.

614
00:27:00,030 --> 00:27:02,513
说... 政府从未授权...
And say... the government has never author...

615
00:27:03,603 --> 00:27:05,381
万一他们发现真相呢?
Supposing they find out the truth?

616
00:27:05,382 --> 00:27:07,574
那你只需说没人告诉你
You'll just have to say that nobody told you

617
00:27:08,887 --> 00:27:13,245
因为你没必要知道 好吗?
because you didn't need to know. Agreed?

618
00:27:14,736 --> 00:27:16,723
太好了 就这么定了
Splendid. Well, That's settled, then.

619
00:27:17,098 --> 00:27:19,799
带子可以物归原主了吗?
May one have one's tapes back?

620
00:27:23,313 --> 00:27:24,450
明天
Tomorrow.

621
00:27:26,762 --> 00:27:29,193
特别委员会质询完之后
After the Committee on Privileges.

622
00:27:29,822 --> 00:27:30,966
好吗 汉弗莱?
All right, Humphrey?

623
00:27:32,110 --> 00:27:33,747
是 首相
Yes, Prime Minister.

624
00:27:34,761 --> 00:27:37,767
<font color="#4096d1">"是,大臣"&"是,首相"系列全剧终
感谢大家19个月以来的支持

625
